# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  zGuard is CLOSED SOURCE.  This directory is the BINARY IMAGE ONLY.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Track ONLY the compiled artifacts (.so / .pyd) + package markers
#  (__init__.py re-export shims, no logic). NEVER track zGuard .py SOURCE here —
#  that is a closed-source LEAK into the public zOS-OpenCore repo.
#
#  zAgent — the image is produced by `zhrsc export` from the private zGuard repo.
#  Edit zGuard logic THERE, export, then `z patch`. If a non-__init__ .py shows
#  up under zguard/ here, it is a mistake — do NOT `git add -f` past this rule.
#  Missing image at runtime → zOS falls back to a local zhrsc install.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Ignore ALL source by default...
*.py

# ...except package markers (required so the binary package imports cleanly).
!__init__.py

# The compiled binary image IS tracked (override any parent rules).
!*.so
!*.pyd
